// If the object being created is a Storage Key and fixedParent is SET in the
// attributes of inPublic, then the symmetric algorithms and parameters of
// inPublic are required to match those of the parent. The algorithms that must
// match are inPublic.nameAlg, and the values in inPublic.parameters that select
// the symmetric scheme. If inPublic.nameAlg does not match, the TPM shall
// return TPM_RC_HASH. If the symmetric scheme of the key does not match, the
// parent, the TPM shall return TPM_RC_SYMMETRIC. The TPM shall not use
// different response code to differentiate between mismatches of the components
// of inPublic.parameters. However, after this verification, when using the
// scheme to encrypt child objects, the TPM ignores the symmetric mode and uses
// TPM_ALG_CFB.
//
// The symmetric scheme is a TPMT_SYM_DEF_OBJECT. In a symmetric block cipher,
// it is at inPublic.parameters.symDetail.sym and in an asymmetric object is at
// inPublic.parameters.asymDetail.symmetric.
TpmTestVector(
  name: "[TPM2_Create] storage key",
  spec_versions: [
    184,
  ],
  test_sequence: [
  ]
)
